{#
  An item's reactions: the current tally, then the six-emoji picker.

  `summary` is a Modules\Groups\Service\ReactionSummary (entries already in
  the fixed display order, with the viewer's own one flagged), `action` the
  POST endpoint, `reactors_url` the GET endpoint behind the tally's own
  click (Controller\ReactionController's `postReactors`/`replyReactors` —
  "who reacted, and with what"), and `compact` switches to the tighter
  variant used under a reply.

  Every button is a real form POST, so this works with no JavaScript at
  all; groups.js upgrades the same POST to a fetch() and swaps this whole
  div with the server's freshly rendered response (Controller\
  ReactionController), so a reaction never reloads the page but still
  waits for the server's answer before showing anything new. The tally
  itself is a plain, unstyled <button> with no JS at all: nothing here
  breaks if groups.js never loads, it just stops being clickable.
#}
{#
  No `flex-wrap` utility here: it is `flex-wrap: wrap !important`, which
  no ordinary rule can turn off — and the open picker on a phone has to
  hold this row to ONE line (components.css). The wrapping this row does
  everywhere else is owned by `.groups-reactions` in that same file, the
  same ownership `display` already moved there for the two blocks below.
#}
<div class="groups-reactions{{ compact ? ' groups-reactions-compact' : '' }} d-flex align-items-center gap-1 mt-2">
    {% if summary.entries is not empty %}
        <button type="button" class="groups-reaction-tally btn btn-link p-0 border-0 d-inline-flex align-items-center gap-1 text-decoration-none"
                data-reactors-url="{{ reactors_url }}" aria-haspopup="dialog">
            {% for entry in summary.entries %}
                <span class="groups-reaction-count{{ entry.is_own ? ' groups-reaction-own' : '' }}"
                      title="{{ entry.count }}">
                    <span aria-hidden="true">{{ entry.emoji }}</span>{{ entry.count }}
                </span>
            {% endfor %}
        </button>
    {% endif %}

    {#
      On a phone the six buttons plus the tally do not fit on one line, so
      they fold behind this one — which only ever appears once groups.js
      has marked the page as able to open it again (`groups-js` on <html>,
      components.css). With no JavaScript this button is never shown and
      the six stay exactly where they have always been: the same posture
      as members.html.twig's invite box, where JS swaps in the richer
      control and its absence leaves the plain one working.

      A real <button type="button"> inside the form's own row but outside
      every form: it submits nothing, it only reveals.
    #}
    <button type="button" class="groups-reaction-toggle btn btn-sm align-items-center gap-1"
            aria-expanded="false">
        <i class="bi bi-emoji-smile" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span>Réagir</span>
    </button>

    {#
      Read straight from Support\Reactions::EMOJI rather than passed in by
      each controller that renders a card: there are three of them, and the
      picker must never be able to drift from the map the server validates
      against.
    #}
    {# No `d-inline-flex` here, nor on the button above: that utility is
       `display: inline-flex !important`, which no ordinary rule can turn
       off — so components.css owns the `display` of both and Bootstrap
       keeps the rest. #}
    <div class="groups-reaction-picker align-items-center gap-1">
        {% for key, emoji in constant('Modules\\Groups\\Support\\Reactions::EMOJI') %}
            <form method="post" action="{{ action }}" class="d-inline groups-reaction-form">
                {{ csrf_field()|raw }}
                <input type="hidden" name="reaction" value="{{ key }}">
                <button type="submit"
                        class="btn btn-sm groups-reaction-btn{{ summary.ownKey == key ? ' groups-reaction-btn-own' : '' }}"
                        aria-label="Réagir : {{ key }}"
                        aria-pressed="{{ summary.ownKey == key ? 'true' : 'false' }}">
                    <span aria-hidden="true">{{ emoji }}</span>
                </button>
            </form>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
</div>
